# secureblue optional/build package list for Omarchy quattro
# Format: one package name per line - system tier (rpm-ostree) only. Unlike
# omarchy-base.packages.secureblue this file carries no gui:/cli: entries;
# everything here is either a runtime shared library the desktop session
# itself links against, or a build-toolchain package other host-level steps
# actually need present (see below) - none of it belongs sandboxed away.
#
# @development-tools (the dnf group) has no rpm-ostree @group syntax to
# resolve it against, so it's spelled out below as an explicit package list
# (a hand-picked approximation of Fedora's "Development Tools" comps group -
# dnf itself can't be queried for the exact current membership here without
# a writable /etc/yum.repos.d, see the secureblue branch of
# install/helpers/fedora-copr.sh for the same access issue).
#
# This intentionally does NOT live in a toolbox instead: fedora-manual.sh's
# starship/eza cargo fallbacks (`cargo install --locked ...`) compile from
# source and shell out to a C compiler as part of that build - if gcc only
# existed inside a toolbox, those host-level cargo builds would have no
# compiler to find. One location for the toolchain, not two.
gcc
gcc-c++
make
automake
autoconf
libtool
rpm-build
redhat-rpm-config
pkgconf-pkg-config
patch
diffutils
findutils
gettext

# Everything else here is the same list as omarchy-other.packages.fedora;
# see that file for the fuller per-package commentary on what's omitted and
# why.
autoconf-archive
btrfs-progs
egl-wayland
pipewire-gstreamer
gtk4-layer-shell
pulseaudio-libs
wpa_supplicant
tiny-dfr
glycin-loaders
wget2-wget
zram-generator
